    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12174" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cynorrŏdon</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-rhŏd-</span></b> ), i,
			n., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-da</span></b> ,
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυνόρροδον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The dog-rose</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rosa canina, Linn. Form -oda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 41, 63, § 152</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">24, 13, 74,
				§ 121</span></i>.—Form -odon, <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 4,
				30, § 94</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 2, 6</span></i>,
			§§ 17 and 18 al. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The blossom of the red lily</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cynorrodon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 5, 11, § 24</span></i>
			.</div>
